WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:00.680
[John:] Good morning, Hank;

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.520
It's Friday!

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.800
It's the final day of Pizzamas 2015.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.260
And, what a ride it's been.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.060
We've laughed,

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.560
we've cried,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.480
we've suited up,

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.660
we've learned some art history;

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:09.980
and, perhaps most importantly,

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.060
we have made the accquaintance of Cheese Doodles Guy.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.300
[Cheese Doodles Guy:] [Screaming] YEAAAHHH!!!

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:17.100
YEAAAAAAAHHHH!!!

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.180
[John:] But, all good things must end;

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.060
even the excitement over cheese doodles.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.020
In fact, come to think of it,

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:21.920
everything must end.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:22.940
In this universe,

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.560
to be is to not always be.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.720
Or, actually, maybe not.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:26.240
Maybe "to be"

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.220
is just "to change".

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:27.780
After all,

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.680
those cheese doodles eventually became poop.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:30.180
But anyway,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:31.100
the end of Pizzamas also means

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.180
that this is the last

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.520
that you can order Pizzamas merch!

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.320
My face in a nebula

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:34.900
on your torso,

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:36.700
only available until midnight tonight

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.160
along with the rest of the Pizzamas merch.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.360
Check it out at dftba.com  ;

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.360
link in the doobly-doo.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:41.400
But, if you leave Pizzamas

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.320
with no physical mementos;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:42.820
fear not.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:43.940
When Nerdfighter D.C.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.140
complained that they were too broke to enjoy Pizzamas,

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.520
Untapped Inkwell replied:

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.520
"Pizzamas is just as much a state of being,

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:51.520
as it is a consumerist holiday."

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:52.620
So true.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.620
So true of all consumerist holidays, actually.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.340
Which, these days,

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.660
is to say all holidays.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.700
But, speaking of states of being;

00:00:57.700 --> 00:00:59.700
you talked about kind of personal stuff in your video yesterday, Hank.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:00.680
So, I guess I'll do the same.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.140
I have a mental illness called

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:03.260
Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder;

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.260
which, is often associated with anxiety

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.520
and depression problems.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.620
I try to talk about that sometimes,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.580
because I don't think that there should be anything embarrassing

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:10.180
about mental illness;

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.600
but, I don't talk about it that much.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:12.800
Because, one: it's personal;

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.680
and two: I find it difficult to talk about my own experiences with chronic illness

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.860
because the central way we imagine sickness,

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.860
as a thing that we must conquer

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.000
and then put behind us,

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.000
doesn't really apply to chronic illness.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.380
Like, when you go to the store

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.920
to get a card for a sick friend;

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.020
you go to the "Get Well Soon" section, right?

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:29.420
But, for people living with chronic illness,

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.060
it often isn't a question of getting "well soon".

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.060
Like Hank, I hope that someday they cure ulcerative colitis;

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.200
but, I don't expect you to "get well soon".

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.400
Instead, my hope for you is that you live a rich and full life;

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.000
and that you aren't marginalized because of your illness.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:42.940
Which is a big problem!

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:43.900
I have a theory about this, Hank;

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:47.340
I don't think we humans like to imagine our lives as "random".

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.700
We need human lives to be narratives that make sense;

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:51.540
so, if we can't find causation,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:52.660
we just create it.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.640
Like, people get depression

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:54.480
because they're weak;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:55.500
or they get diabetes,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.460
because they don't eat well;

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.460
or they have heart failure,

00:01:57.460 --> 00:01:58.920
because they don't exercise.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:01:59.420
All of that stuff

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.660
is either totally inaccurate

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:01.780
or overly simplistic,

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:04.380
but we want every effect to have a cause;

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.200
and, when we can't find that cause,

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.180
we invent one.

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.180
Anyway Hank, as you know,

00:02:08.180 --> 00:02:09.900
I have been very sick over the last several weeks

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.900
as I've tried to figure out a new medication regimen.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:13.120
Over the years of living with my illness,

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.280
I've learned about how to make it tolerable.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.980
I've learned to celebrate small successes;

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.600
I've learned to encourage myself without being cruel.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.320
And, most importantly,

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:21.380
I've learned that there is hope;

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.000
and that when I feel like there isn't hope,

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:24.280
my brain is lying to me.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:24.860
But still,

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:25.820
it is awful!

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:27.600
And, after years of relatively good health,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:29.600
I have been reminded in the last several weeks

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:30.980
just how painful

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:32.920
and crushing that this stuff can be.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.120
And, that's despite my having all kinds of advantages that make it easier to live with;

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.780
an incredibly supportive family,

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.220
total job flexibility,

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:40.840
an excellent therapist and psychiatrist,

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:42.200
money to afford medication,

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:42.800
etcetera.

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:44.400
Most people don't have all of those resources,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.060
and that worsens any kind of illness.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.380
Hank, I've mentioned all of this for three reasons.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.700
First, to tell people who may be living with mental illness

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.640
that there is hope.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.860
That mental illness is almost always treatable;

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.140
and that, how you feel when you are at your sickest

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.960
is not how you will always feel.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.840
And, down in the doobly doo,

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:59.840
you can find the links to resources that I've found helpful,

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.240
and that the people I know have found helpful.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.440
Secondly, I want to remind all of us,

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.100
that what we see in videos or on Instagram

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.320
isn't the whole story.

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:08.660
Like, my friends and family have known that I have been unwell over the last several weeks,

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:11.140
because it is impossible for me to hide it from them;

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.080
but, it is very possible for me to hide it with jump cuts.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.620
And lastly, to say thanks!

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.240
Thank you for watching these videos;

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.180
and Hank, thank you for the gift of Pizzamas,

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.560
which has given structure and achieveable tasks to my life

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.560
at a time when I desperately needed them.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:26.860
I'm starting to feel better for a variety of reasons;

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:28.160
from medication to exercise.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:31.460
But, the gift of Pizzamas has been surprisingly important;

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:33.220
so, thank you for being a part of it.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:33.940
Hank;

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.120
Don't forget to be awesome!

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.340
I will see you-

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:36.860
No!!

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.860
No; you will see me

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.860
on Tuesday.

